Z||000003||theogre||07-04-2001||11:11 PM||||I use 10-30 Mobile 1. Started using it several months ago in an engine over 150,000 miles. Car likes it just fine. current load is way cleaner than crude based stuff even after 3 months.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 07-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Buster||07-05-2001||05:49 PM||||My 88 has 73K. I am going to use the Valvoline high mileage 10W30. I have been using it in my 94 Lumina van 3.1 with 100K.<BR>It seems to have helped that cold start puff of smoke from the valve seals. One note I have the same cold puff ( large puff occasionally ) from my motorcycle I have had for 5 yrs, 1985. I don't ride hard enough and I believe the oil ring gets gummed up. Once a year I put a can of Casite detergent additive in for 200 miles prior to an oil change and it definitely helps.||||reg||1
